//! Conformance harness entry. Wires the helpers (`_helpers.rs`) and the
//! per-case tests (`_generated.rs`, `_generated_operators.rs`) into a single cargo
//! integration-test binary: fixed predicates and EvalContexts whose verdicts the
//! contract must keep.
//!
//! Run with:
//!   cargo test --test conformance -p policy-interpreter
//!
//! The cases were generated by a TypeScript synthesiser and reference
//! evaluator that are not part of this tree (the TypeScript side has no
//! evaluator: simulate and verify call the contract's own `check`), so the
//! files are kept as they are and are not regenerated. The cross-layer gate for
//! the wire format is `tests/parity.rs`, which writes the corpus the TypeScript
//! codec is tested against (`packages/policy-synth/fixtures/parity/grammar.json`).
//!
//! `_generated.rs` covers the predicate a recording synthesises.
//! `_generated_operators.rs` covers `or`, `lt`, `gt` and `gte`, which the
//! recording path cannot reach: its deny-case mutators cannot violate a scaled
//! bound, and they skip `or` because violating one branch proves nothing while
//! another can still permit.

mod _generated;
mod _generated_operators;
mod _helpers;
